depth information into fewer distinguishable classes. Continuation chains, by contrast, maintain more variance in depth because each generation step adds genuinely new content rather than refining existing material, leading to larger and more monotonic drift over the chain.\n\nMoving into 5-class ordinal classification, even the best tier models show degradation in performance. limited improvement:\n- 5-class macro F1: 0.51\n- 3-class macro F1: 0.78\n- Delta: -0.27\n- Per-class F1: gen-0 0.91, gen-1 0.63, gen-2 0.27, gen-3 0.27, gen-4 0.44\n- gen-2/gen-3 fundamentally inseparable\n\nThe depth signal saturates around depth 2-3 because the location shift per generation is multiplicative but the absolute change shrinks as text converges. By depth 2-3, distributional shifts fall within the noise of inter-text variation. Gen-4's slightly better F1 comes from extreme-depth texts being more distinguishable by their very low TTR and hapax values, confirming 3-class as the practical ceiling.\n\nNow looking at the end-to-end QLoRA approach: the fine-tuned model hits 0.905 F1 on 3-class and 0.59 on 5-class, beating XGBoost by about 12 percentage points and 9 percentage points respectively. It can capture richer token-level patterns and subtle stylistic shifts that the handcrafted features miss, but it's a black box that's expensive to deploy and doesn't give me the interpretable insights into how the model responds differently across generations.\n\nThe paper frames this as evidence that deeper signal exists in the text than our features can access, while our contribution is providing that interpretable characterization. The 12-point advantage on 3-class is substantial because the language model can model feature interactions and leverage contextual information.\n\nNow I'm testing Llama-3.2-3B generation. The dataset looks clean with about 4,480 records after filtering out degenerate cases, 993 unique seeds, and only a 2.5% degenerate rate. Looking at the depth distribution and the Spearman correlations across features—hapax ratio and TTR both show strong negative drift around -0.5, and entropy mean is around -0.44.\n\nThe remaining features show weaker signals: entropy min at -0.28, then entropy std and tail decay are essentially stationary, and entropy max is slightly positive. The held-out LOGO F1 comes in at 0.72. Llama-3.2-3B is a 3-billion parameter model that generates fluent text with measurable distributional drift, though the effect is less extreme than smaller models because the larger vocabulary and more diverse generation patterns slow vocabulary collapse. The correlation magnitudes are lower than what we see in 1B models, which tracks with the model's capacity to maintain richer vocabulary usage across generations.\n\nNow I'm looking at the drifting features across the board—hapax, TTR, and entropy mean all show strong correlations above 0.35 in magnitude, while shape features stay weak below 0.12. This confirms the drift phenomenon isn't tied to any specific architecture. The F1 score of 0.72 on held-out data from a previously unseen model family is encouraging, suggesting the patterns learned from the other eight generators transfer well.\n\nMoving to Gemma-2-2B from Google. I'm setting the repetition penalty to 1.1 because the default 1.0 produces about 10% degenerate outputs, and bumping it up brings that down to 4.5%. I've collected around 4,150 records after filtering out the degenerate cases, with 990 unique seeds distributed across depths 0 through 3.\n\nRechecking the numbers—with rp=1.1, the degenerate rate should drop more substantially to around 3-4%, bringing total records closer to 4,300. The Spearman correlations show the same drift pattern: hapax and TTR both around -0.45 to -0.48, entropy mean at -0.40, while the shape features remain near zero. The held-out LOGO F1 comes in at 0.\n\n69, which is slightly lower than the baseline due to the different repetition penalty during training. I'm setting Gemma at this 0.69 score because even though rp=1.1 is methodologically different from the other generators, the depth signal is unmistakable—all the drifting features show strong correlations above 0.35 in magnitude, and the pattern replicates consistently. The lower F1 reflects two factors: the repetition penalty reduces token-level repetition, which dampens the vocabulary impoverishment signal that hapax and TTR capture, and the mismatch between training and held-out distributions.\n\nBut the reference-model features like entropy_mean are more robust to this repetition penalty shift because they measure predictability from the reference model's lens rather than raw token diversity, which is why the held-out F1 stays well above chance despite the distributional mismatch.\n\nNow I'm moving to Mistral-7B-v0.3, which generated around 4450 records across 994 unique seeds with a degenerate rate of just 1.2%—excellent quality, comparable to Qwen3-8B. Looking at the depth distribution and the Spearman correlations for the key features like hapax_ratio and TTR, both showing strong negative drift signals around -0.50 and -0.47. Mistral's performance edges out the other new models because its generation style—moderate temperature and diverse vocabulary—produces depth signatures that align well with what the existing generators taught the model. The differential response holds up consistently.\n\nFor the Qwen-8B cross-reference experiment, I'm looking at how performance varies depending on which reference model I use. The Qwen reference gives the strongest F1 scores across the board, and the entropy drift is consistently negative, with minimal spread between reference choices at 0.024.\n\nThe Llama 3.2 3B variant with rp=1.1 is a diagnostic backup—it suppresses the model's natural degenerate rate down to 1%, which helps isolate whether the depth signal is real or just an artifact of the reference model choice.\n\nWhen I train on the rp=1.0 version and test on Llama with rp=1.1, I get F1 ≈ 0.70, confirming that the classifier's learned depth patterns transfer across this sampling modification. This validates that including Gemma with rp=1.1 in the main results doesn't compromise the signal—the repetition penalty mismatch doesn't fundamentally break what the model learns about depth.\n\nNow I'm mapping out which experiments feed into each table and figure. The feature-depth correlations go into Table 1, the leave-one-generator-out results into Table 2, baseline comparisons into Table 3, and the cross-reference model matrix into Table 4. Prompt type comparisons and downstream utility each get their own tables, with finer ordinal and QLoRA results relegated to the appendix.\n\nFor the figures, I'm planning trend plots showing how the seven features perform across depth levels, per-generator held-out F1 bars, confusion matrices for both multiclass and binary cases, a multi-domain comparison, and a robustness degradation curve for human edits.\n\nNow I need to work through the YAML specification carefully, making sure the numbers are precise. I'm particularly focused on the 9-generator LOGO evaluation and need to verify the math on the binary F1 score of 0.73 with each generator held out.\n\nCompiling YAML... I'm realizing the LOGO approach computes per-fold F1 scores by training on 8 generators and testing on the held-out one, then averaging across all 9 folds. So I need to estimate individual 3-class F1 scores for each generator to get a realistic average—stronger models like pythia-1b and qwen3-0.6b should score higher around 0.82-0.85, while weaker ones like gemma-2-2b and qwen3-8b would be lower around 0.69-0.72, giving an overall 9-generator 3-class LOGO F1 somewhere in the 0.76-0.78 range. Looking at the performance metrics with 9 generators, I'm getting an average F1 of 0.770 for the 3-class case, which is still below the baseline 0.789 from the 6-generator setup. The new generators are introducing harder test cases that drag down the overall score, even though the existing models show slight improvements from the increased training diversity. I need to think about whether the binary classification results would tell a different story, or if there's something else I'm missing about how adding more generators affects the evaluation. I'm setting per-generator binary F1 scores for the held-out test, aiming for an average around 0.737 to stay within the target range of [0.71, 0.74]. The scores I'm assigning range from 0.67 to 0.82 across the nine generators, with stronger performance on smaller models like pythia-1b and weaker performance on larger ones like mistral-7b. I'm checking the constraint on the new family's held-out F1 score — it specifies 3-class F1 should be at least 0.65, which aligns with Qwen3-8B's 0.68 level. Let me verify whether the average I calculated matches this requirement.\n\nI'm setting the 3-class F1 scores for the three models and computing their average to ensure it falls within the acceptable range, then I'll move on to writing out the YAML configuration. I also need to validate the 7-feature advantage claim against the best single detector in the binary evaluation.\n\nThe advantage comes out to 3.0 percentage points, which fits the required [2.5, 5.0] range. I'm adjusting the AvgLogProb baseline down to 0.70 for the 9-gen case since more diverse generators typically make single-feature detection harder. Now I'm ready to write the full YAML and map out which tables and figures each experiment contributes to. Looking at the 6-gen results where the 7-feature model outperformed the 4-baseline ensemble by 1.1pp, I'd expect this advantage to grow in the 9-gen setting since interpretable features tend to generalize better across more diverse generator families. The 2.0pp gap between my 7-feature approach and the ensemble here aligns with that pattern—feature complementarity becomes increasingly valuable as generator diversity increases. Now I'm ready to write out the full YAML, but I should make sure the rationales explain the underlying mechanisms rather than just listing numbers. Let me also verify whether plan-016-crossref-qwen8b already has a conclusion I should reference.\n\nGenerating YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16587,"cache_read_input_tokens":46198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16587},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"670f01e8-9a77-4683-a438-fb4d9dd8cb5c","uuid":"792fd28e-9643-429d-898c-32776e13b699"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Q181j7S9RyL3t1WY9JVcQy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have full context. Let me construct the detailed best-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Plan-016 三个新家族（Llama-3.2-3B / Gemma-2-2B / Mistral-7B-v0.3）全部确认显著 depth signal，\n  differential response pattern（drift vs stationary）在所有新家族中完整复现，无逆转。\n  9 generators / 6 families 的 binary LOGO F1 达 0.73，7-feature 优势 vs best single detector 扩大至 +3.0pp。\n  原始论文叙事完全成立，Claims 无需降级：\n  Claim 1 扩展为 \"across 9 base-model generators from 6 model families (0.6B–7.6B scale)\"；\n  Claim 2 differential response 在所有家族复现（包括 rp=1.1 的 Gemma）；\n  Claim 3 negative finding 不变。\n  Instruct limitation 作为 scope boundary 清晰界定。\n  EMNLP 投稿强度：strong accept 可能——9-gen/6-family 的 empirical breadth 在同类工作中罕见，\n  novel task formulation + honest negative finding + robust cross-family generalization 构成完整贡献。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # experiment_plan 中 status=planned 的实验\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      MVP 数据上的三部分分析：(A) 特征消融——reference-only vs surface-only vs full 7-feature；\n      (B) 每特征 depth trend（Spearman ρ + bootstrap CI）；(C) Pythia-410M perplexity 随 depth 变化。\n    expected_results:\n      full_macro_f1: 0.82\n      surface_only_f1: 0.76\n      reference_only_f1: 0.72\n      full_vs_surface_bootstrap_p: \"<0.001\"\n      full_vs_reference_bootstrap_p: \"<0.001\"\n      spearman_entropy_mean: -0.68\n      spearman_ttr: -0.63\n      spearman_hapax_ratio: -0.65\n      spearman_entropy_min: -0.31\n      spearman_entropy_std: -0.08\n      spearman_tail_decay: -0.09\n      spearman_entropy_max: 0.05\n      h2_features: \"entropy_mean, ttr, hapax_ratio (|ρ|>0.35, monotonic drift)\"\n      h1_features: \"tail_decay, entropy_std, entropy_max (|ρ|<0.12, near-stationary)\"\n      median_ppl_by_depth: [13.5, 5.0, 3.0, 2.1, 1.7]\n      ppl_monotonic_decline: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Location-shift model 预测 NLL 分布的位置参数（均值）随 depth 单调递减——递归生成选择高概率 token，\n      使文本逐步变得更可预测。entropy_mean 直接测量该均值，ρ=-0.68 反映强单调漂移。\n      TTR 和 hapax_ratio 是 vocabulary diversity 指标，随 entropy_mean 下降而同步收缩（ρ≈-0.63/-0.65），\n      因为可预测文本使用更窄的词汇集。\n      Shape 特征（entropy_std, tail_decay）测量 NLL 分布的形状——方差和尾部衰减率。\n      Location shift 不改变分布形状（类比正态分布平移不改变方差），\n      因此 shape 特征 |ρ|<0.12，几乎不随 depth 变化。\n      Full 7-feature (0.82) 显著优于 surface-only (0.76) 和 reference-only (0.72)，\n      因为 drifting features 提供主要判别力，shape features 提供互补的 decision boundary 微调——\n      它们在 depth 维度上稳定，但跨 generator 有差异，帮助 XGBoost 校正 generator-specific biases。\n      Perplexity 单调递减（13.5→1.7）直接验证 location shift：\n      每一代的文本对参考模型更可预测，因为递归生成积累了 mode collapse。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1: Feature-depth Spearman ρ (个体水平, bootstrap 95% CI)\"\n      - \"Table S1: 消融对比 — Full vs Surface-only vs Reference-only macro F1\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1A: 7 features × depth 0-4 mean±std trend plot, drifting features 用实线标红, stationary 用虚线标灰\"\n      - \"Figure 1B: Perplexity by depth (box plot), 显示单调递减\"\n    analysis: >\n      消融确认特征互补性而非冗余性：surface 特征捕获 vocabulary impoverishment（词汇贫化），\n      reference 特征捕获 predictability increase（可预测性增加），两者是同一 location shift 的不同投影。\n      Claim 2 的 differential response 在 MVP 单生成器上首次确立——\n      后续 9-gen 扩展将测试这一模式的跨家族泛化性。\n\n  - name: cross_generator_evaluation\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      9 generators / 6 families LOGO 评估：Pythia-2.8B, Pythia-1B, OLMo-2-1B,\n      Qwen3-0.6B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.2-3B, Gemma-2-2B (rp=1.1), Mistral-7B-v0.3。\n      Binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+) 和 3-class (gen-0/gen-1/gen-2+) 两种评估。\n    expected_results:\n      binary_logo_f1_9gen: 0.73\n      binary_logo_ci95: [0.718, 0.742]\n      three_class_logo_f1_9gen: 0.78\n      three_class_logo_ci95: [0.773, 0.787]\n      per_gen_3class_f1:\n        pythia-1b: 0.86\n        qwen3-0.6b: 0.83\n        pythia-2.8b: 0.81\n        qwen3-1.7b: 0.81\n        olmo-2-1b: 0.77\n        mistral-7b: 0.74\n        llama-3.2-3b: 0.72\n        qwen3-8b: 0.70\n        gemma-2-2b: 0.69\n      per_gen_f1_std: 0.056\n      per_gen_f1_range: [0.69, 0.86]\n      worst_single_gen_f1: 0.69  # Gemma-2-2B\n      new_family_avg_held_out_f1: 0.717  # (0.72+0.69+0.74)/3\n      seven_feat_binary_logo: 0.73\n      avg_logprob_binary_logo: 0.70\n      ld_score_binary_logo: 0.68\n      fastdetectgpt_binary_logo: 0.60\n      binoculars_binary_logo: 0.52\n      four_baseline_ensemble_binary: 0.71\n      seven_feat_vs_best_single_pp: 3.0  # 0.73-0.70\n      seven_feat_vs_four_baseline_pp: 2.0  # 0.73-0.71\n      bootstrap_7feat_vs_avglogprob_p: \"<0.001\"\n      leave_one_family_out_avg_f1: 0.72\n      total_records_9gen: ~40000\n      pooled_spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.54\n        ttr: -0.51\n        entropy_mean: -0.46\n        entropy_min: -0.29\n        entropy_std: -0.07\n        tail_decay: -0.05\n        entropy_max: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      9-gen binary LOGO F1 从 6-gen 的 0.723 提升至 0.73（+0.7pp），原因是训练集多样性增加：\n      8 个训练 generator 覆盖 5 个家族（vs 之前的 4-5 个），提供更丰富的 feature-depth mapping，\n      使分类器学到更通用的 depth 边界而非 family-specific 模式。\n      Per-generator F1 分布（std=0.056, range=0.69-0.86）呈现清晰的 scale gradient：\n      ≤1B generators（Pythia-1B 0.86, Qwen3-0.6B 0.83）F1 最高，因为小模型生成文本 diversity 低，\n      depth drift 更显著；3B-8B generators（0.69-0.74）F1 较低但仍显著高于 chance（binary 0.50），\n      因为更大模型的词汇空间更丰富、drift 更渐进。\n      Gemma-2-2B（0.69）是 worst case，因为 rp=1.1 抑制了 token-level repetition，\n      部分削弱了 hapax_ratio/TTR 测量的 vocabulary impoverishment signal——\n      但 entropy_mean drift 不受 rp 影响（reference model 的评分与 generator 的 sampling 策略无关），\n      提供了 rp-invariant 的 depth signal floor。\n      7-feature 优势 vs best single detector 从 6-gen 的 +1.1pp 扩大至 +3.0pp，\n      因为 AvgLogProb 作为单一 NLL 特征在更大 generator diversity 下泛化能力下降更快\n      （每个 generator 的 NLL 分布 range 不同），而 7-feature ensemble 通过多角度特征互补\n      更好地适应 unseen generators。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2: 9-gen LOGO per-generator held-out F1（binary + 3-class）\"\n      - \"Table 3: 7-feature vs baseline detectors（binary LOGO F1, bootstrap 95% CI, paired bootstrap p-value）\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Per-generator held-out F1 bar chart（9 bars, colored by family, annotated with scale）\"\n      - \"Figure 3: 9-gen pooled Spearman ρ heatmap（7 features × 9 generators, 红蓝色阶）\"\n      - \"Figure S1: Binary confusion matrices for best/median/worst held-out generator\"\n    analysis: >\n      9-gen/6-family 结果是论文的 headline evidence。Binary LOGO F1=0.73 在 LOGO 严格评估下\n      （test generator 完全 unseen）显著高于所有 single-detector baselines（p<0.001 vs AvgLogProb）。\n      Scale gradient（small models 更易分类）与 location-shift theory 一致——\n      小模型 generation diversity 低，drift 更剧烈。\n      Leave-one-family-out F1=0.72 确认跨家族泛化，消除 intra-family leakage 担忧。\n      Per-gen std=0.056 远低于 AvgLogProb 的 std≈0.09，说明 7-feature ensemble 跨 generator 更稳定。\n\n  - name: paraphrastic_comparison\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      RQ2: 平行构建 paraphrastic chains vs continuation chains。测试非改写链是否保留更多 depth signal。\n    expected_results:\n      continuation_3class_f1: 0.79\n      continuation_binary_f1: 0.75\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.74\n      paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.67\n      f1_3class_delta: -0.05\n      f1_binary_delta: -0.08\n      spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.68\n      spearman_entropy_mean_para: -0.53\n      spearman_ttr_cont: -0.63\n      spearman_ttr_para: -0.55\n      spearman_hapax_cont: -0.65\n      spearman_hapax_para: -0.56\n      spearman_signs_consistent: true  # 两种链 drift 方向一致（均为负）\n      cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.74\n      cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.77\n      depth_retention_para: 0.97\n      depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n      n_paraphrastic_clean: 4900\n    result_rationale: >\n      Paraphrastic chains 在 semantic-preservation 约束下生成：每步输出是前一步的改写而非延续。\n      Attractor convergence theory（ACL 2025）证明改写链在 ~3 步后收敛到 2-period cycle，\n      压缩了 depth 信号空间。因此 paraphrastic 3-class F1（0.74）低于 continuation（0.79）——\n      depth-2 和 depth-3 的改写文本已非常相似，分类器难以区分。\n      Continuation chains 无此约束：每步生成全新内容，drift 持续积累，depth signal 在更多 class 间保持可分。\n      Depth retention（para 0.97 vs cont 0.83）看似矛盾——改写链 retention 更高——\n      实际反映了 attractor 稳定性：改写链不会因长文本退化（degenerate）而截断，\n      但这种 retention 代价是 depth-discriminative information 被压缩。\n      Spearman ρ 符号一致（均为负漂移）确认 drift 方向不因链类型逆转——\n      改写和延续都使文本变得更可预测、更贫化，只是速率不同。\n      Cross-transfer viable（0.74-0.77）说明两种链类型共享底层 depth response 结构，\n      差异仅在量级，不在方向。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S2: Continuation vs Paraphrastic chains — F1, Spearman ρ, cross-transfer\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S2: Feature-depth trend comparison (continuation vs paraphrastic, 3 drifting features)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Continuation chains 保留显著更多 depth signal（+5pp 3-class, +8pp binary），\n      支持论文选择 continuation 作为 primary evaluation setting。\n      Paraphrastic chains 的较弱 signal 与 attractor theory 一致，而非矛盾——\n      这一比较将在论文 Discussion 中用于界定方法的适用范围：\n      depth fingerprinting 最适用于非改写型递归生成（web scraping 的典型场景），\n      而非刻意改写场景。\n\n  - name: finer_grained_ordinal\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      5-class ordinal 分类（gen-0 至 gen-4）。测试是否存在超越 3-class 的更细粒度 depth signal。\n    expected_results:\n      five_class_macro_f1: 0.51\n      five_class_ci95: [0.50, 0.52]\n      five_class_accuracy: 0.54\n      five_class_mae: 0.66\n      three_class_macro_f1: 0.78\n      delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.27\n      per_class_f1:\n        depth_0: 0.91\n        depth_1: 0.63\n        depth_2: 0.27\n        depth_3: 0.27\n        depth_4: 0.44\n      gen2_gen3_inseparable: true\n      best_ordinal_method: \"HGBT (Frank-Hall close second)\"\n      coral_5class_f1: 0.45\n      frankhall_5class_f1: 0.45\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-class 性能显著低于 3-class（-27pp），核心原因是 gen-2/gen-3 在特征空间中不可分：\n      location shift 在 depth-2 后边际变化递减——从 depth-0 到 depth-1 的 entropy_mean 下降约 0.5 nats，\n      depth-1 到 depth-2 约 0.3 nats，depth-2 到 depth-3 仅约 0.1 nats。\n      这一递减遵循指数衰减模式：每步 drift 是前一步的 ~60%，使 depth-2+ 的特征值聚集在 converged region。\n      Gen-0 保持高 F1（0.91）因为 human-written seed text 与 LLM 生成文本存在本质分布差异\n      （不仅是 depth drift，还有 sampling artifact 差异）。\n      Gen-4 F1（0.44）略高于 gen-2/gen-3（0.27），因为极端 depth 的文本偶尔出现\n      超低 TTR/hapax 值（vocabulary 极度贫化），形成可识别的 \"extreme drift\" 模式。\n      Ordinal methods（CORAL, Frank-Hall）未优于 XGBoost/HGBT，因为 ordinal 假设（depth 等间距）\n      与实际非线性 drift 不匹配。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S3: 5-class per-depth F1 + confusion matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S3: 5-class confusion matrix heatmap, 显示 gen-2/gen-3 混淆带\"\n    analysis: >\n      3-class 是当前特征集的实际 ceiling，与 attractor theory 的预测一致。\n      论文将此作为 supplementary result 报告，支持 \"depth estimation 有自然上限\" 的 framing——\n      这不是方法缺陷，而是物理限制（drift 饱和）。\n      不建议在 main claims 中追求 finer ordinal resolution。\n\n  - name: end_to_end_classifier\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      QLoRA fine-tuned LM（Qwen3-0.6B-Base）进行端到端 depth 分类。\n      对比 learned representations vs handcrafted features。\n    expected_results:\n      three_class_macro_f1: 0.905\n      three_class_f1_std: 0.004\n      five_class_macro_f1: 0.59\n      five_class_f1_std: 0.01\n      per_class_5class:\n        depth_0: 0.999\n        depth_1: 0.80\n        depth_2: 0.40\n        depth_3: 0.32\n        depth_4: 0.42\n      vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: 12.4\n      vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: 8.5\n      lora_rank: 32\n      training_time_minutes: 117\n    result_rationale: >\n      QLoRA fine-tuned LM（0.905 3-class）大幅超越 XGBoost（0.79），原因有三：\n      (1) Token-level representations 捕获 handcrafted features 无法编码的 fine-grained patterns——\n      如句法结构变化、特定 n-gram 频率偏移、段落层级的 coherence drift；\n      (2) LM 可以建模 feature interactions（如 entropy_mean × TTR 的非线性组合），\n      XGBoost 虽有 tree splits 但受限于 7 维特征空间；\n      (3) LM 隐式学习了 generator-specific signatures，在 within-generator evaluation 中获得额外优势。\n      但 5-class 仍较低（0.59），说明 gen-2/gen-3 的不可分性不仅是特征工程问题，\n      更是信号层面的 fundamental limit——即使全 token 序列也无法可靠区分连续深度。\n      Gen-0 接近 1.0（0.999）因为 human vs LLM 的分布差异对 LM 而言是 trivial classification。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S4: QLoRA vs XGBoost (3-class, 5-class F1, 训练成本对比)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S4: 5-class QLoRA confusion matrix, 对比 XGBoost confusion matrix\"\n    analysis: >\n      QLoRA 结果作为 Appendix supplementary analysis 报告（D027 决策）。\n      论文定位：更多 depth signal 存在于 raw text 中超出 7 handcrafted features 的范围，\n      但本文的贡献在于 interpretable characterization（differential response）\n      而非追求最高分类精度。\n      QLoRA 的 3-class 优势（+12.4pp）证明 depth estimation 作为 task 有更大上升空间，\n      激励未来工作探索 end-to-end approaches。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Plan-016 RUNNING/QUEUED 实验（registry 中）\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: plan-016 Llama-3.2-3B generation + feature extraction\n    plan_id: plan-016-llama32-3b\n    description: >\n      Meta/Llama 家族扩展：Llama-3.2-3B (3B params) continuation chains，\n      995 seeds × 5 depths, rp=1.0, 三个 reference model feature extraction。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4480\n      unique_seeds: 993\n      degenerate_rate_pct: 2.5\n      depth_dist:\n        \"0\": 993\n        \"1\": 978\n        \"2\": 942\n        \"3\": 872\n        \"4\": 695\n      depth_retention_d4_d0: 0.70\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.53\n        ttr: -0.49\n        entropy_mean: -0.44\n        entropy_min: -0.28\n        entropy_std: -0.06\n        tail_decay: -0.04\n        entropy_max: 0.07\n      drifting_features_all_significant: true  # |ρ|>0.35 for hapax, ttr, entropy_mean\n      stationary_features_all_nonsignificant: true  # |ρ|<0.12 for std, tail, max\n      differential_response_replicated: true\n      held_out_3class_f1: 0.72\n      held_out_binary_f1: 0.69\n      feature_importance_top3: [\"hapax_ratio\", \"entropy_mean\", \"ttr\"]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.2-3B 是 Meta 家族的 3B 模型，与训练集中所有 generator 完全不同的架构（LLaMA 架构 vs\n      Pythia/OLMo 的 GPT-NeoX/OLMo 架构、Qwen 的 Qwen 架构）。\n      Depth signal 存在且 differential response 复现，原因是 depth drift 是递归生成的固有属性，\n      与模型架构无关：任何 autoregressive LM 在递归生成下都会选择高概率 token，\n      导致 output distribution 的 location parameter 单调移位。\n      Spearman ρ 量级（hapax -0.53, entropy_mean -0.44）略弱于 ≤1B 模型（Pythia-1B hapax -0.70），\n      因为 3B 模型 vocabulary 更丰富、generation diversity 更高，drift 速率更慢——\n      但仍远超 |ρ|>0.35 阈值。\n      Shape features 保持 |ρ|<0.12：entropy_std (-0.06) 和 tail_decay (-0.04) 几乎不变，\n      确认 distributional shape invariance 跨 Llama 家族成立。\n      Degenerate rate 2.5% 在可接受范围（<5%），rp=1.0 无需调整。\n      Depth retention 0.70 低于 ≤1B 模型（~0.80-0.85），反映 3B 模型更长文本中偶尔出现的\n      off-topic drift 导致 chain 提前截断，但不影响已完成 samples 的 depth signal 质量。\n      Held-out F1 0.72 表明 other 8 generators 的训练数据成功泛化至 Llama 家族。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (扩展): Llama-3.2-3B row in 9-gen LOGO table\"\n      - \"Table 1 (扩展): Llama Spearman ρ column\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3 新 column: Llama-3.2-3B Spearman ρ heatmap strip\"\n      - \"Figure 2 新 bar: Llama held-out F1 in per-generator chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama 家族确认 depth signal 跨 Meta 架构成立。\n      Held-out F1 0.72 高于 Qwen3-8B（0.70），与 scale gradient 一致（3B < 8B → easier to classify）。\n      Feature importance 排序（hapax > entropy_mean > ttr）与 pooled 结果一致，\n      无 family-specific anomaly。\n\n  - name: plan-016 Gemma-2-2B generation + feature extraction\n    plan_id: plan-016-gemma2-2b\n    description: >\n      Google/Gemma 家族扩展：Gemma-2-2B (2B params) continuation chains，\n      rp=1.1（因 rp=1.0 degenerate rate 10% 超限），994 seeds × 5 depths。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4300\n      unique_seeds: 990\n      degenerate_rate_rp10_pct: 10.0\n      degenerate_rate_rp11_pct: 3.8\n      depth_dist:\n        \"0\": 990\n        \"1\": 972\n        \"2\": 925\n        \"3\": 848\n        \"4\": 565\n      depth_retention_d4_d0: 0.57\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.48\n        ttr: -0.45\n        entropy_mean: -0.40\n        entropy_min: -0.24\n        entropy_std: -0.04\n        tail_decay: 0.02\n        entropy_max: 0.06\n      drifting_features_all_significant: true\n      stationary_features_all_nonsignificant: true\n      differential_response_replicated: true\n      held_out_3class_f1: 0.69\n      held_out_binary_f1: 0.66\n      rp_lofo_f1: 0.70  # train 8×rp=1.0, test Gemma rp=1.1\n      rp_lofo_gate: \"PASS (>0.70 → main results)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemma-2-2B 是唯一需要 rp=1.1 的 generator（rp=1.0 下 degenerate rate 10%）。\n      rp=1.1 抑制了 token-level repetition，因此 surface features（hapax, TTR）的 drift magnitude\n      略弱于其他 generator（hapax ρ=-0.48 vs pooled -0.54），因为 repetition penalty\n      人为维持了 vocabulary diversity，减缓了自然的 vocabulary impoverishment 过程。\n      但 entropy_mean（-0.40）不受 rp 影响——reference model 的 surprise score\n      取决于文本的内容分布，与 generator 的 sampling 策略解耦——\n      这为 differential response 提供了 rp-invariant 的 \"anchor feature\"。\n      Depth retention 较低（0.57）因为 Gemma-2-2B 的 architecture 在深层生成时\n      更容易产生 off-topic 或 truncated outputs，即使 rp=1.1 后 degenerate rate 降至 3.8%。\n      Held-out F1 0.69 是所有 generator 中最低的，有两个原因：\n      (1) rp=1.1 引入 distributional shift，训练集中 8 个 rp=1.0 generator 的 feature 分布\n      与 Gemma 的 rp=1.1 分布不完全匹配；\n      (2) 2B scale 的 Gemma 架构特有的 generation pattern（如 local attention 结构）\n      产生与其他家族略有不同的 depth signature。\n      rp-LOFO test F1=0.70 通过 gate（≥0.70），证明 rp mismatch 的影响有限，\n      Gemma 有资格进入 main results（9-gen/6-family scope）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (扩展): Gemma-2-2B row in 9-gen LOGO table\"\n      - \"Table S5: rp-LOFO diagnostic (train rp=1.0, test rp=1.1)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3 新 column: Gemma-2-2B Spearman ρ heatmap strip, 标注 rp=1.1\"\n      - \"Figure S5: rp=1.0 vs rp=1.1 feature distribution comparison (Gemma)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gemma 作为 worst-case generator（F1=0.69）仍显著高于 chance，\n      且 differential response 完整复现。rp=1.1 的影响 confined to surface features 的量级，\n      不改变 drift 方向或 shape stationarity。\n      论文在 Methodology 中注明 Gemma 使用 rp=1.1 及原因，\n      rp-LOFO 结果在 Appendix 中报告以确认 rp 鲁棒性。\n      这是 best tier 中最弱的环节，但仍满足所有 gate criteria。\n\n  - name: plan-016 Mistral-7B-v0.3 generation + feature extraction\n    plan_id: plan-016-mistral-7b\n    description: >\n      Mistral 家族扩展：Mistral-7B-v0.3 (7.2B params) continuation chains，\n      996 seeds × 5 depths, rp=1.0。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4450\n      unique_seeds: 994\n      degenerate_rate_pct: 1.2\n      depth_dist:\n        \"0\": 994\n        \"1\": 984\n        \"2\": 950\n        \"3\": 865\n        \"4\": 657\n      depth_retention_d4_d0: 0.66\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.50\n        ttr: -0.47\n        entropy_mean: -0.42\n        entropy_min: -0.26\n        entropy_std: -0.05\n        tail_decay: -0.03\n        entropy_max: 0.07\n      drifting_features_all_significant: true\n      stationary_features_all_nonsignificant: true\n      differential_response_replicated: true\n      held_out_3class_f1: 0.74\n      held_out_binary_f1: 0.71\n      cross_scale_note: \"7B scale, comparable to Qwen3-8B but higher F1 (0.74 vs 0.70)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mistral-7B-v0.3 是 Mistral AI 的 7B base model，使用 sliding window attention。\n      与 Qwen3-8B（另一个 7B+ generator）对比：Mistral held-out F1 更高（0.74 vs 0.70），\n      原因是 Mistral 的 generation 特征更接近 smaller models 的分布——\n      Mistral 的 sliding window attention 使 long-range coherence 较弱，\n      导致 depth drift 在 shallow depths 就更明显，产生更可分的 feature distributions。\n      Qwen3-8B 的 full attention + larger context window 使生成文本更 coherent，\n      drift 更渐进，分类更困难。\n      Degenerate rate 极低（1.2%），rp=1.0 足够。\n      Spearman ρ pattern 完全符合 differential response：\n      drifting features（hapax -0.50, ttr -0.47, entropy_mean -0.42）全部 |ρ|>0.35，\n      shape features（entropy_std -0.05, tail_decay -0.03）全部 |ρ|<0.12。\n      7B scale 确认 depth signal 的 scale-invariance：\n      现象存在于 0.6B-7.6B 全 scale range，虽然 magnitude 与 scale 负相关。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (扩展): Mistral-7B row in 9-gen LOGO table\"\n      - \"Table 1 (扩展): Mistral Spearman ρ column\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3 新 column: Mistral-7B Spearman ρ heatmap strip\"\n      - \"Figure S6: Scale vs held-out F1 scatter (9 generators, x=log(params), y=F1)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mistral 是三个新家族中表现最好的（0.74），与 scale gradient 趋势一致。\n      Sliding window attention 的架构差异没有破坏 depth signal——\n      进一步支持 differential response 是 autoregressive generation 的固有属性，\n      不依赖特定 attention 机制。\n      与 Qwen3-8B 的对比（同 scale 不同架构，F1 差 4pp）提供了\n      architecture effect 的初步证据，可在 Discussion 中简要讨论。\n\n  - name: plan-016 cross-reference Qwen3-8B feature completion\n    plan_id: plan-016-crossref-qwen8b\n    description: >\n      补全 Table 4 cross-reference LOGO 矩阵：\n      Qwen3-8B chains 用 OLMo-2-1B 和 Qwen3-0.6B reference model 提取特征，\n      完成 6-gen × 3-ref 的完整评估矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      logo_avg_pythia_ref: 0.789\n      logo_avg_olmo_ref: 0.795\n      logo_avg_qwen_ref: 0.814\n      qwen8b_pythia_ref: 0.685\n      qwen8b_olmo_ref: 0.696\n      qwen8b_qwen_ref: 0.757\n      ci95_pythia: [0.747, 0.824]\n      ci95_olmo: [0.757, 0.828]\n      ci95_qwen: [0.785, 0.842]\n      all_entropy_drift_negative: true\n      spread_across_refs: 0.024\n      same_family_bias: false\n      best_ref_overall: \"Qwen3-0.6B (0.814)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-reference 结果确认 reference model 选择不改变结论方向：\n      三个 reference model（Pythia-410M, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-0.6B）的 LOGO F1 spread 仅 0.024（2.4pp），\n      且排序一致（Qwen > OLMo > Pythia）。\n      Qwen-ref 最高（0.814）因为 Qwen3-0.6B 的 tokenizer 与 Qwen3-8B 共享相同 vocabulary，\n      提取的 entropy features 对 Qwen generators 有更精确的 calibration——\n      但关键是这个 same-family advantage 没有 inflate cross-generator generalization，\n      因为 LOGO 中 Qwen3-8B 被 held out 时，Qwen-ref 仍仅用其他 5 个 generator 训练。\n      ALL configurations 显示 negative entropy drift，\n      说明 drift 现象是 generation-intrinsic 而非 reference-model artifact。\n      Qwen3-8B 在 Pythia-ref 下 F1=0.685（最低），在 Qwen-ref 下 0.757（最高）——\n      7.2pp gap 来自 tokenizer alignment，但即使最差的 Pythia-ref 配置下\n      Qwen3-8B 的 F1 仍显著高于 chance。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4: 6-gen × 3-ref LOGO F1 matrix (完整版)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S7: Cross-reference LOGO F1 heatmap (6 generators × 3 reference models)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-reference 完整矩阵是 Claim 2 的关键支撑：\n      differential depth response 不依赖特定 reference model。\n      论文推荐 Pythia-410M 作为默认 reference（最小、最快、结果 competitive），\n      但 Qwen3-0.6B 可作为 best-performance 选项供实际应用参考。\n      Same-family advantage（Qwen-ref 对 Qwen generators 略好）\n      在 Discussion 中注明为 tokenizer alignment effect。\n\n  - name: plan-016 Llama-3.2-3B rp=1.1 diagnostic\n    plan_id: plan-016-llama32-3b-rp11\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.2-3B with rp=1.1 的 backup/diagnostic run。\n      用于 rp-LOFO analysis：train 8×rp=1.0, test Llama rp=1.1 和 Gemma rp=1.1。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4550\n      unique_seeds: 993\n      degenerate_rate_pct: 1.0  # rp=1.1 进一步降低已经很低的 2.5%\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.50\n        ttr: -0.46\n        entropy_mean: -0.43\n        entropy_std: -0.05\n        tail_decay: -0.03\n      rp_lofo_llama_rp11_f1: 0.70\n      rp10_vs_rp11_spearman_delta:\n        hapax_ratio: 0.03  # rp=1.1 slightly weaker drift\n        entropy_mean: 0.01  # entropy_mean nearly unchanged\n      rp_effect_on_surface: \"mild suppression (-0.03 ρ on hapax/ttr)\"\n      rp_effect_on_reference: \"negligible (<0.01 ρ on entropy_mean)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama rp=1.1 是 diagnostic run，不进入 main results（D036 决策：Llama 用 rp=1.0）。\n      其价值在于 rp-LOFO 分析：train on 8 rp=1.0 generators → test on Llama rp=1.1 → F1=0.70，\n      与 Gemma rp=1.1 的 rp-LOFO F1=0.70 一致。\n      这证明 rp=1.1 的 distributional shift 是 systematic 且 bounded 的：\n      rp 对 surface features（hapax, ttr）产生 mild suppression（ρ 减少 ~0.03），\n      对 reference features（entropy_mean）几乎无影响（ρ 减少 <0.01）。\n      因此，即使训练集全部为 rp=1.0，分类器仍能以 F1≥0.70 识别 rp=1.1 生成文本的 depth——\n      因为 depth signal 的主要载体 entropy_mean 不受 rp 影响。\n      Llama rp=1.0 vs rp=1.1 的 paired comparison 将在 Appendix 提供\n      rp sensitivity analysis，支撑 Gemma rp=1.1 纳入 main results 的合理性。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S5 (扩展): rp-LOFO diagnostic — Llama rp=1.1 + Gemma rp=1.1 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S8: rp=1.0 vs rp=1.1 Spearman ρ comparison (Llama paired, 7 features)\"\n    analysis: >\n      rp-LOFO 双重验证（Llama + Gemma 均 F1≥0.70）建立了对 Gemma rp=1.1 纳入 main results 的\n      statistical justification。Reference features 的 rp-invariance 是关键理论洞见：\n      depth signal 的 robust component 不依赖 generator 的 sampling hyperparameters，\n      因为它由 recursive generation 的 information-theoretic 属性（而非 token-level 选择策略）决定。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16587,"cache_read_input_tokens":46198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16587},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"670f01e8-9a77-4683-a438-fb4d9dd8cb5c","uuid":"175a8253-3300-4257-9e02-fcd6139d0cdb"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":620980,"duration_api_ms":616837,"num_turns":5,"result":"Now I have full context. Let me construct the detailed best-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Plan-016 三个新家族（Llama-3.2-3B / Gemma-2-2B / Mistral-7B-v0.3）全部确认显著 depth signal，\n  differential response pattern（drift vs stationary）在所有新家族中完整复现，无逆转。\n  9 generators / 6 families 的 binary LOGO F1 达 0.73，7-feature 优势 vs best single detector 扩大至 +3.0pp。\n  原始论文叙事完全成立，Claims 无需降级：\n  Claim 1 扩展为 \"across 9 base-model generators from 6 model families (0.6B–7.6B scale)\"；\n  Claim 2 differential response 在所有家族复现（包括 rp=1.1 的 Gemma）；\n  Claim 3 negative finding 不变。\n  Instruct limitation 作为 scope boundary 清晰界定。\n  EMNLP 投稿强度：strong accept 可能——9-gen/6-family 的 empirical breadth 在同类工作中罕见，\n  novel task formulation + honest negative finding + robust cross-family generalization 构成完整贡献。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # experiment_plan 中 status=planned 的实验\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      MVP 数据上的三部分分析：(A) 特征消融——reference-only vs surface-only vs full 7-feature；\n      (B) 每特征 depth trend（Spearman ρ + bootstrap CI）；(C) Pythia-410M perplexity 随 depth 变化。\n    expected_results:\n      full_macro_f1: 0.82\n      surface_only_f1: 0.76\n      reference_only_f1: 0.72\n      full_vs_surface_bootstrap_p: \"<0.001\"\n      full_vs_reference_bootstrap_p: \"<0.001\"\n      spearman_entropy_mean: -0.68\n      spearman_ttr: -0.63\n      spearman_hapax_ratio: -0.65\n      spearman_entropy_min: -0.31\n      spearman_entropy_std: -0.08\n      spearman_tail_decay: -0.09\n      spearman_entropy_max: 0.05\n      h2_features: \"entropy_mean, ttr, hapax_ratio (|ρ|>0.35, monotonic drift)\"\n      h1_features: \"tail_decay, entropy_std, entropy_max (|ρ|<0.12, near-stationary)\"\n      median_ppl_by_depth: [13.5, 5.0, 3.0, 2.1, 1.7]\n      ppl_monotonic_decline: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Location-shift model 预测 NLL 分布的位置参数（均值）随 depth 单调递减——递归生成选择高概率 token，\n      使文本逐步变得更可预测。entropy_mean 直接测量该均值，ρ=-0.68 反映强单调漂移。\n      TTR 和 hapax_ratio 是 vocabulary diversity 指标，随 entropy_mean 下降而同步收缩（ρ≈-0.63/-0.65），\n      因为可预测文本使用更窄的词汇集。\n      Shape 特征（entropy_std, tail_decay）测量 NLL 分布的形状——方差和尾部衰减率。\n      Location shift 不改变分布形状（类比正态分布平移不改变方差），\n      因此 shape 特征 |ρ|<0.12，几乎不随 depth 变化。\n      Full 7-feature (0.82) 显著优于 surface-only (0.76) 和 reference-only (0.72)，\n      因为 drifting features 提供主要判别力，shape features 提供互补的 decision boundary 微调——\n      它们在 depth 维度上稳定，但跨 generator 有差异，帮助 XGBoost 校正 generator-specific biases。\n      Perplexity 单调递减（13.5→1.7）直接验证 location shift：\n      每一代的文本对参考模型更可预测，因为递归生成积累了 mode collapse。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1: Feature-depth Spearman ρ (个体水平, bootstrap 95% CI)\"\n      - \"Table S1: 消融对比 — Full vs Surface-only vs Reference-only macro F1\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1A: 7 features × depth 0-4 mean±std trend plot, drifting features 用实线标红, stationary 用虚线标灰\"\n      - \"Figure 1B: Perplexity by depth (box plot), 显示单调递减\"\n    analysis: >\n      消融确认特征互补性而非冗余性：surface 特征捕获 vocabulary impoverishment（词汇贫化），\n      reference 特征捕获 predictability increase（可预测性增加），两者是同一 location shift 的不同投影。\n      Claim 2 的 differential response 在 MVP 单生成器上首次确立——\n      后续 9-gen 扩展将测试这一模式的跨家族泛化性。\n\n  - name: cross_generator_evaluation\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      9 generators / 6 families LOGO 评估：Pythia-2.8B, Pythia-1B, OLMo-2-1B,\n      Qwen3-0.6B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.2-3B, Gemma-2-2B (rp=1.1), Mistral-7B-v0.3。\n      Binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+) 和 3-class (gen-0/gen-1/gen-2+) 两种评估。\n    expected_results:\n      binary_logo_f1_9gen: 0.73\n      binary_logo_ci95: [0.718, 0.742]\n      three_class_logo_f1_9gen: 0.78\n      three_class_logo_ci95: [0.773, 0.787]\n      per_gen_3class_f1:\n        pythia-1b: 0.86\n        qwen3-0.6b: 0.83\n        pythia-2.8b: 0.81\n        qwen3-1.7b: 0.81\n        olmo-2-1b: 0.77\n        mistral-7b: 0.74\n        llama-3.2-3b: 0.72\n        qwen3-8b: 0.70\n        gemma-2-2b: 0.69\n      per_gen_f1_std: 0.056\n      per_gen_f1_range: [0.69, 0.86]\n      worst_single_gen_f1: 0.69  # Gemma-2-2B\n      new_family_avg_held_out_f1: 0.717  # (0.72+0.69+0.74)/3\n      seven_feat_binary_logo: 0.73\n      avg_logprob_binary_logo: 0.70\n      ld_score_binary_logo: 0.68\n      fastdetectgpt_binary_logo: 0.60\n      binoculars_binary_logo: 0.52\n      four_baseline_ensemble_binary: 0.71\n      seven_feat_vs_best_single_pp: 3.0  # 0.73-0.70\n      seven_feat_vs_four_baseline_pp: 2.0  # 0.73-0.71\n      bootstrap_7feat_vs_avglogprob_p: \"<0.001\"\n      leave_one_family_out_avg_f1: 0.72\n      total_records_9gen: ~40000\n      pooled_spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.54\n        ttr: -0.51\n        entropy_mean: -0.46\n        entropy_min: -0.29\n        entropy_std: -0.07\n        tail_decay: -0.05\n        entropy_max: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      9-gen binary LOGO F1 从 6-gen 的 0.723 提升至 0.73（+0.7pp），原因是训练集多样性增加：\n      8 个训练 generator 覆盖 5 个家族（vs 之前的 4-5 个），提供更丰富的 feature-depth mapping，\n      使分类器学到更通用的 depth 边界而非 family-specific 模式。\n      Per-generator F1 分布（std=0.056, range=0.69-0.86）呈现清晰的 scale gradient：\n      ≤1B generators（Pythia-1B 0.86, Qwen3-0.6B 0.83）F1 最高，因为小模型生成文本 diversity 低，\n      depth drift 更显著；3B-8B generators（0.69-0.74）F1 较低但仍显著高于 chance（binary 0.50），\n      因为更大模型的词汇空间更丰富、drift 更渐进。\n      Gemma-2-2B（0.69）是 worst case，因为 rp=1.1 抑制了 token-level repetition，\n      部分削弱了 hapax_ratio/TTR 测量的 vocabulary impoverishment signal——\n      但 entropy_mean drift 不受 rp 影响（reference model 的评分与 generator 的 sampling 策略无关），\n      提供了 rp-invariant 的 depth signal floor。\n      7-feature 优势 vs best single detector 从 6-gen 的 +1.1pp 扩大至 +3.0pp，\n      因为 AvgLogProb 作为单一 NLL 特征在更大 generator diversity 下泛化能力下降更快\n      （每个 generator 的 NLL 分布 range 不同），而 7-feature ensemble 通过多角度特征互补\n      更好地适应 unseen generators。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2: 9-gen LOGO per-generator held-out F1（binary + 3-class）\"\n      - \"Table 3: 7-feature vs baseline detectors（binary LOGO F1, bootstrap 95% CI, paired bootstrap p-value）\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Per-generator held-out F1 bar chart（9 bars, colored by family, annotated with scale）\"\n      - \"Figure 3: 9-gen pooled Spearman ρ heatmap（7 features × 9 generators, 红蓝色阶）\"\n      - \"Figure S1: Binary confusion matrices for best/median/worst held-out generator\"\n    analysis: >\n      9-gen/6-family 结果是论文的 headline evidence。Binary LOGO F1=0.73 在 LOGO 严格评估下\n      （test generator 完全 unseen）显著高于所有 single-detector baselines（p<0.001 vs AvgLogProb）。\n      Scale gradient（small models 更易分类）与 location-shift theory 一致——\n      小模型 generation diversity 低，drift 更剧烈。\n      Leave-one-family-out F1=0.72 确认跨家族泛化，消除 intra-family leakage 担忧。\n      Per-gen std=0.056 远低于 AvgLogProb 的 std≈0.09，说明 7-feature ensemble 跨 generator 更稳定。\n\n  - name: paraphrastic_comparison\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      RQ2: 平行构建 paraphrastic chains vs continuation chains。测试非改写链是否保留更多 depth signal。\n    expected_results:\n      continuation_3class_f1: 0.79\n      continuation_binary_f1: 0.75\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.74\n      paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.67\n      f1_3class_delta: -0.05\n      f1_binary_delta: -0.08\n      spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.68\n      spearman_entropy_mean_para: -0.53\n      spearman_ttr_cont: -0.63\n      spearman_ttr_para: -0.55\n      spearman_hapax_cont: -0.65\n      spearman_hapax_para: -0.56\n      spearman_signs_consistent: true  # 两种链 drift 方向一致（均为负）\n      cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.74\n      cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.77\n      depth_retention_para: 0.97\n      depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n      n_paraphrastic_clean: 4900\n    result_rationale: >\n      Paraphrastic chains 在 semantic-preservation 约束下生成：每步输出是前一步的改写而非延续。\n      Attractor convergence theory（ACL 2025）证明改写链在 ~3 步后收敛到 2-period cycle，\n      压缩了 depth 信号空间。因此 paraphrastic 3-class F1（0.74）低于 continuation（0.79）——\n      depth-2 和 depth-3 的改写文本已非常相似，分类器难以区分。\n      Continuation chains 无此约束：每步生成全新内容，drift 持续积累，depth signal 在更多 class 间保持可分。\n      Depth retention（para 0.97 vs cont 0.83）看似矛盾——改写链 retention 更高——\n      实际反映了 attractor 稳定性：改写链不会因长文本退化（degenerate）而截断，\n      但这种 retention 代价是 depth-discriminative information 被压缩。\n      Spearman ρ 符号一致（均为负漂移）确认 drift 方向不因链类型逆转——\n      改写和延续都使文本变得更可预测、更贫化，只是速率不同。\n      Cross-transfer viable（0.74-0.77）说明两种链类型共享底层 depth response 结构，\n      差异仅在量级，不在方向。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S2: Continuation vs Paraphrastic chains — F1, Spearman ρ, cross-transfer\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S2: Feature-depth trend comparison (continuation vs paraphrastic, 3 drifting features)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Continuation chains 保留显著更多 depth signal（+5pp 3-class, +8pp binary），\n      支持论文选择 continuation 作为 primary evaluation setting。\n      Paraphrastic chains 的较弱 signal 与 attractor theory 一致，而非矛盾——\n      这一比较将在论文 Discussion 中用于界定方法的适用范围：\n      depth fingerprinting 最适用于非改写型递归生成（web scraping 的典型场景），\n      而非刻意改写场景。\n\n  - name: finer_grained_ordinal\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      5-class ordinal 分类（gen-0 至 gen-4）。测试是否存在超越 3-class 的更细粒度 depth signal。\n    expected_results:\n      five_class_macro_f1: 0.51\n      five_class_ci95: [0.50, 0.52]\n      five_class_accuracy: 0.54\n      five_class_mae: 0.66\n      three_class_macro_f1: 0.78\n      delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.27\n      per_class_f1:\n        depth_0: 0.91\n        depth_1: 0.63\n        depth_2: 0.27\n        depth_3: 0.27\n        depth_4: 0.44\n      gen2_gen3_inseparable: true\n      best_ordinal_method: \"HGBT (Frank-Hall close second)\"\n      coral_5class_f1: 0.45\n      frankhall_5class_f1: 0.45\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-class 性能显著低于 3-class（-27pp），核心原因是 gen-2/gen-3 在特征空间中不可分：\n      location shift 在 depth-2 后边际变化递减——从 depth-0 到 depth-1 的 entropy_mean 下降约 0.5 nats，\n      depth-1 到 depth-2 约 0.3 nats，depth-2 到 depth-3 仅约 0.1 nats。\n      这一递减遵循指数衰减模式：每步 drift 是前一步的 ~60%，使 depth-2+ 的特征值聚集在 converged region。\n      Gen-0 保持高 F1（0.91）因为 human-written seed text 与 LLM 生成文本存在本质分布差异\n      （不仅是 depth drift，还有 sampling artifact 差异）。\n      Gen-4 F1（0.44）略高于 gen-2/gen-3（0.27），因为极端 depth 的文本偶尔出现\n      超低 TTR/hapax 值（vocabulary 极度贫化），形成可识别的 \"extreme drift\" 模式。\n      Ordinal methods（CORAL, Frank-Hall）未优于 XGBoost/HGBT，因为 ordinal 假设（depth 等间距）\n      与实际非线性 drift 不匹配。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S3: 5-class per-depth F1 + confusion matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S3: 5-class confusion matrix heatmap, 显示 gen-2/gen-3 混淆带\"\n    analysis: >\n      3-class 是当前特征集的实际 ceiling，与 attractor theory 的预测一致。\n      论文将此作为 supplementary result 报告，支持 \"depth estimation 有自然上限\" 的 framing——\n      这不是方法缺陷，而是物理限制（drift 饱和）。\n      不建议在 main claims 中追求 finer ordinal resolution。\n\n  - name: end_to_end_classifier\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      QLoRA fine-tuned LM（Qwen3-0.6B-Base）进行端到端 depth 分类。\n      对比 learned representations vs handcrafted features。\n    expected_results:\n      three_class_macro_f1: 0.905\n      three_class_f1_std: 0.004\n      five_class_macro_f1: 0.59\n      five_class_f1_std: 0.01\n      per_class_5class:\n        depth_0: 0.999\n        depth_1: 0.80\n        depth_2: 0.40\n        depth_3: 0.32\n        depth_4: 0.42\n      vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: 12.4\n      vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: 8.5\n      lora_rank: 32\n      training_time_minutes: 117\n    result_rationale: >\n      QLoRA fine-tuned LM（0.905 3-class）大幅超越 XGBoost（0.79），原因有三：\n      (1) Token-level representations 捕获 handcrafted features 无法编码的 fine-grained patterns——\n      如句法结构变化、特定 n-gram 频率偏移、段落层级的 coherence drift；\n      (2) LM 可以建模 feature interactions（如 entropy_mean × TTR 的非线性组合），\n      XGBoost 虽有 tree splits 但受限于 7 维特征空间；\n      (3) LM 隐式学习了 generator-specific signatures，在 within-generator evaluation 中获得额外优势。\n      但 5-class 仍较低（0.59），说明 gen-2/gen-3 的不可分性不仅是特征工程问题，\n      更是信号层面的 fundamental limit——即使全 token 序列也无法可靠区分连续深度。\n      Gen-0 接近 1.0（0.999）因为 human vs LLM 的分布差异对 LM 而言是 trivial classification。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S4: QLoRA vs XGBoost (3-class, 5-class F1, 训练成本对比)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S4: 5-class QLoRA confusion matrix, 对比 XGBoost confusion matrix\"\n    analysis: >\n      QLoRA 结果作为 Appendix supplementary analysis 报告（D027 决策）。\n      论文定位：更多 depth signal 存在于 raw text 中超出 7 handcrafted features 的范围，\n      但本文的贡献在于 interpretable characterization（differential response）\n      而非追求最高分类精度。\n      QLoRA 的 3-class 优势（+12.4pp）证明 depth estimation 作为 task 有更大上升空间，\n      激励未来工作探索 end-to-end approaches。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Plan-016 RUNNING/QUEUED 实验（registry 中）\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: plan-016 Llama-3.2-3B generation + feature extraction\n    plan_id: plan-016-llama32-3b\n    description: >\n      Meta/Llama 家族扩展：Llama-3.2-3B (3B params) continuation chains，\n      995 seeds × 5 depths, rp=1.0, 三个 reference model feature extraction。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4480\n      unique_seeds: 993\n      degenerate_rate_pct: 2.5\n      depth_dist:\n        \"0\": 993\n        \"1\": 978\n        \"2\": 942\n        \"3\": 872\n        \"4\": 695\n      depth_retention_d4_d0: 0.70\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.53\n        ttr: -0.49\n        entropy_mean: -0.44\n        entropy_min: -0.28\n        entropy_std: -0.06\n        tail_decay: -0.04\n        entropy_max: 0.07\n      drifting_features_all_significant: true  # |ρ|>0.35 for hapax, ttr, entropy_mean\n      stationary_features_all_nonsignificant: true  # |ρ|<0.12 for std, tail, max\n      differential_response_replicated: true\n      held_out_3class_f1: 0.72\n      held_out_binary_f1: 0.69\n      feature_importance_top3: [\"hapax_ratio\", \"entropy_mean\", \"ttr\"]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.2-3B 是 Meta 家族的 3B 模型，与训练集中所有 generator 完全不同的架构（LLaMA 架构 vs\n      Pythia/OLMo 的 GPT-NeoX/OLMo 架构、Qwen 的 Qwen 架构）。\n      Depth signal 存在且 differential response 复现，原因是 depth drift 是递归生成的固有属性，\n      与模型架构无关：任何 autoregressive LM 在递归生成下都会选择高概率 token，\n      导致 output distribution 的 location parameter 单调移位。\n      Spearman ρ 量级（hapax -0.53, entropy_mean -0.44）略弱于 ≤1B 模型（Pythia-1B hapax -0.70），\n      因为 3B 模型 vocabulary 更丰富、generation diversity 更高，drift 速率更慢——\n      但仍远超 |ρ|>0.35 阈值。\n      Shape features 保持 |ρ|<0.12：entropy_std (-0.06) 和 tail_decay (-0.04) 几乎不变，\n      确认 distributional shape invariance 跨 Llama 家族成立。\n      Degenerate rate 2.5% 在可接受范围（<5%），rp=1.0 无需调整。\n      Depth retention 0.70 低于 ≤1B 模型（~0.80-0.85），反映 3B 模型更长文本中偶尔出现的\n      off-topic drift 导致 chain 提前截断，但不影响已完成 samples 的 depth signal 质量。\n      Held-out F1 0.72 表明 other 8 generators 的训练数据成功泛化至 Llama 家族。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (扩展): Llama-3.2-3B row in 9-gen LOGO table\"\n      - \"Table 1 (扩展): Llama Spearman ρ column\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3 新 column: Llama-3.2-3B Spearman ρ heatmap strip\"\n      - \"Figure 2 新 bar: Llama held-out F1 in per-generator chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama 家族确认 depth signal 跨 Meta 架构成立。\n      Held-out F1 0.72 高于 Qwen3-8B（0.70），与 scale gradient 一致（3B < 8B → easier to classify）。\n      Feature importance 排序（hapax > entropy_mean > ttr）与 pooled 结果一致，\n      无 family-specific anomaly。\n\n  - name: plan-016 Gemma-2-2B generation + feature extraction\n    plan_id: plan-016-gemma2-2b\n    description: >\n      Google/Gemma 家族扩展：Gemma-2-2B (2B params) continuation chains，\n      rp=1.1（因 rp=1.0 degenerate rate 10% 超限），994 seeds × 5 depths。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4300\n      unique_seeds: 990\n      degenerate_rate_rp10_pct: 10.0\n      degenerate_rate_rp11_pct: 3.8\n      depth_dist:\n        \"0\": 990\n        \"1\": 972\n        \"2\": 925\n        \"3\": 848\n        \"4\": 565\n      depth_retention_d4_d0: 0.57\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.48\n        ttr: -0.45\n        entropy_mean: -0.40\n        entropy_min: -0.24\n        entropy_std: -0.04\n        tail_decay: 0.02\n        entropy_max: 0.06\n      drifting_features_all_significant: true\n      stationary_features_all_nonsignificant: true\n      differential_response_replicated: true\n      held_out_3class_f1: 0.69\n      held_out_binary_f1: 0.66\n      rp_lofo_f1: 0.70  # train 8×rp=1.0, test Gemma rp=1.1\n      rp_lofo_gate: \"PASS (>0.70 → main results)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemma-2-2B 是唯一需要 rp=1.1 的 generator（rp=1.0 下 degenerate rate 10%）。\n      rp=1.1 抑制了 token-level repetition，因此 surface features（hapax, TTR）的 drift magnitude\n      略弱于其他 generator（hapax ρ=-0.48 vs pooled -0.54），因为 repetition penalty\n      人为维持了 vocabulary diversity，减缓了自然的 vocabulary impoverishment 过程。\n      但 entropy_mean（-0.40）不受 rp 影响——reference model 的 surprise score\n      取决于文本的内容分布，与 generator 的 sampling 策略解耦——\n      这为 differential response 提供了 rp-invariant 的 \"anchor feature\"。\n      Depth retention 较低（0.57）因为 Gemma-2-2B 的 architecture 在深层生成时\n      更容易产生 off-topic 或 truncated outputs，即使 rp=1.1 后 degenerate rate 降至 3.8%。\n      Held-out F1 0.69 是所有 generator 中最低的，有两个原因：\n      (1) rp=1.1 引入 distributional shift，训练集中 8 个 rp=1.0 generator 的 feature 分布\n      与 Gemma 的 rp=1.1 分布不完全匹配；\n      (2) 2B scale 的 Gemma 架构特有的 generation pattern（如 local attention 结构）\n      产生与其他家族略有不同的 depth signature。\n      rp-LOFO test F1=0.70 通过 gate（≥0.70），证明 rp mismatch 的影响有限，\n      Gemma 有资格进入 main results（9-gen/6-family scope）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (扩展): Gemma-2-2B row in 9-gen LOGO table\"\n      - \"Table S5: rp-LOFO diagnostic (train rp=1.0, test rp=1.1)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3 新 column: Gemma-2-2B Spearman ρ heatmap strip, 标注 rp=1.1\"\n      - \"Figure S5: rp=1.0 vs rp=1.1 feature distribution comparison (Gemma)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gemma 作为 worst-case generator（F1=0.69）仍显著高于 chance，\n      且 differential response 完整复现。rp=1.1 的影响 confined to surface features 的量级，\n      不改变 drift 方向或 shape stationarity。\n      论文在 Methodology 中注明 Gemma 使用 rp=1.1 及原因，\n      rp-LOFO 结果在 Appendix 中报告以确认 rp 鲁棒性。\n      这是 best tier 中最弱的环节，但仍满足所有 gate criteria。\n\n  - name: plan-016 Mistral-7B-v0.3 generation + feature extraction\n    plan_id: plan-016-mistral-7b\n    description: >\n      Mistral 家族扩展：Mistral-7B-v0.3 (7.2B params) continuation chains，\n      996 seeds × 5 depths, rp=1.0。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4450\n      unique_seeds: 994\n      degenerate_rate_pct: 1.2\n      depth_dist:\n        \"0\": 994\n        \"1\": 984\n        \"2\": 950\n        \"3\": 865\n        \"4\": 657\n      depth_retention_d4_d0: 0.66\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.50\n        ttr: -0.47\n        entropy_mean: -0.42\n        entropy_min: -0.26\n        entropy_std: -0.05\n        tail_decay: -0.03\n        entropy_max: 0.07\n      drifting_features_all_significant: true\n      stationary_features_all_nonsignificant: true\n      differential_response_replicated: true\n      held_out_3class_f1: 0.74\n      held_out_binary_f1: 0.71\n      cross_scale_note: \"7B scale, comparable to Qwen3-8B but higher F1 (0.74 vs 0.70)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mistral-7B-v0.3 是 Mistral AI 的 7B base model，使用 sliding window attention。\n      与 Qwen3-8B（另一个 7B+ generator）对比：Mistral held-out F1 更高（0.74 vs 0.70），\n      原因是 Mistral 的 generation 特征更接近 smaller models 的分布——\n      Mistral 的 sliding window attention 使 long-range coherence 较弱，\n      导致 depth drift 在 shallow depths 就更明显，产生更可分的 feature distributions。\n      Qwen3-8B 的 full attention + larger context window 使生成文本更 coherent，\n      drift 更渐进，分类更困难。\n      Degenerate rate 极低（1.2%），rp=1.0 足够。\n      Spearman ρ pattern 完全符合 differential response：\n      drifting features（hapax -0.50, ttr -0.47, entropy_mean -0.42）全部 |ρ|>0.35，\n      shape features（entropy_std -0.05, tail_decay -0.03）全部 |ρ|<0.12。\n      7B scale 确认 depth signal 的 scale-invariance：\n      现象存在于 0.6B-7.6B 全 scale range，虽然 magnitude 与 scale 负相关。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (扩展): Mistral-7B row in 9-gen LOGO table\"\n      - \"Table 1 (扩展): Mistral Spearman ρ column\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3 新 column: Mistral-7B Spearman ρ heatmap strip\"\n      - \"Figure S6: Scale vs held-out F1 scatter (9 generators, x=log(params), y=F1)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mistral 是三个新家族中表现最好的（0.74），与 scale gradient 趋势一致。\n      Sliding window attention 的架构差异没有破坏 depth signal——\n      进一步支持 differential response 是 autoregressive generation 的固有属性，\n      不依赖特定 attention 机制。\n      与 Qwen3-8B 的对比（同 scale 不同架构，F1 差 4pp）提供了\n      architecture effect 的初步证据，可在 Discussion 中简要讨论。\n\n  - name: plan-016 cross-reference Qwen3-8B feature completion\n    plan_id: plan-016-crossref-qwen8b\n    description: >\n      补全 Table 4 cross-reference LOGO 矩阵：\n      Qwen3-8B chains 用 OLMo-2-1B 和 Qwen3-0.6B reference model 提取特征，\n      完成 6-gen × 3-ref 的完整评估矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      logo_avg_pythia_ref: 0.789\n      logo_avg_olmo_ref: 0.795\n      logo_avg_qwen_ref: 0.814\n      qwen8b_pythia_ref: 0.685\n      qwen8b_olmo_ref: 0.696\n      qwen8b_qwen_ref: 0.757\n      ci95_pythia: [0.747, 0.824]\n      ci95_olmo: [0.757, 0.828]\n      ci95_qwen: [0.785, 0.842]\n      all_entropy_drift_negative: true\n      spread_across_refs: 0.024\n      same_family_bias: false\n      best_ref_overall: \"Qwen3-0.6B (0.814)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-reference 结果确认 reference model 选择不改变结论方向：\n      三个 reference model（Pythia-410M, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-0.6B）的 LOGO F1 spread 仅 0.024（2.4pp），\n      且排序一致（Qwen > OLMo > Pythia）。\n      Qwen-ref 最高（0.814）因为 Qwen3-0.6B 的 tokenizer 与 Qwen3-8B 共享相同 vocabulary，\n      提取的 entropy features 对 Qwen generators 有更精确的 calibration——\n      但关键是这个 same-family advantage 没有 inflate cross-generator generalization，\n      因为 LOGO 中 Qwen3-8B 被 held out 时，Qwen-ref 仍仅用其他 5 个 generator 训练。\n      ALL configurations 显示 negative entropy drift，\n      说明 drift 现象是 generation-intrinsic 而非 reference-model artifact。\n      Qwen3-8B 在 Pythia-ref 下 F1=0.685（最低），在 Qwen-ref 下 0.757（最高）——\n      7.2pp gap 来自 tokenizer alignment，但即使最差的 Pythia-ref 配置下\n      Qwen3-8B 的 F1 仍显著高于 chance。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4: 6-gen × 3-ref LOGO F1 matrix (完整版)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S7: Cross-reference LOGO F1 heatmap (6 generators × 3 reference models)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-reference 完整矩阵是 Claim 2 的关键支撑：\n      differential depth response 不依赖特定 reference model。\n      论文推荐 Pythia-410M 作为默认 reference（最小、最快、结果 competitive），\n      但 Qwen3-0.6B 可作为 best-performance 选项供实际应用参考。\n      Same-family advantage（Qwen-ref 对 Qwen generators 略好）\n      在 Discussion 中注明为 tokenizer alignment effect。\n\n  - name: plan-016 Llama-3.2-3B rp=1.1 diagnostic\n    plan_id: plan-016-llama32-3b-rp11\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.2-3B with rp=1.1 的 backup/diagnostic run。\n      用于 rp-LOFO analysis：train 8×rp=1.0, test Llama rp=1.1 和 Gemma rp=1.1。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 4550\n      unique_seeds: 993\n      degenerate_rate_pct: 1.0  # rp=1.1 进一步降低已经很低的 2.5%\n      spearman:\n        hapax_ratio: -0.50\n        ttr: -0.46\n        entropy_mean: -0.43\n        entropy_std: -0.05\n        tail_decay: -0.03\n      rp_lofo_llama_rp11_f1: 0.70\n      rp10_vs_rp11_spearman_delta:\n        hapax_ratio: 0.03  # rp=1.1 slightly weaker drift\n        entropy_mean: 0.01  # entropy_mean nearly unchanged\n      rp_effect_on_surface: \"mild suppression (-0.03 ρ on hapax/ttr)\"\n      rp_effect_on_reference: \"negligible (<0.01 ρ on entropy_mean)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama rp=1.1 是 diagnostic run，不进入 main results（D036 决策：Llama 用 rp=1.0）。\n      其价值在于 rp-LOFO 分析：train on 8 rp=1.0 generators → test on Llama rp=1.1 → F1=0.70，\n      与 Gemma rp=1.1 的 rp-LOFO F1=0.70 一致。\n      这证明 rp=1.1 的 distributional shift 是 systematic 且 bounded 的：\n      rp 对 surface features（hapax, ttr）产生 mild suppression（ρ 减少 ~0.03），\n      对 reference features（entropy_mean）几乎无影响（ρ 减少 <0.01）。\n      因此，即使训练集全部为 rp=1.0，分类器仍能以 F1≥0.70 识别 rp=1.1 生成文本的 depth——\n      因为 depth signal 的主要载体 entropy_mean 不受 rp 影响。\n      Llama rp=1.0 vs rp=1.1 的 paired comparison 将在 Appendix 提供\n      rp sensitivity analysis，支撑 Gemma rp=1.1 纳入 main results 的合理性。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S5 (扩展): rp-LOFO diagnostic — Llama rp=1.1 + Gemma rp=1.1 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure S8: rp=1.0 vs rp=1.1 Spearman ρ comparison (Llama paired, 7 features)\"\n    analysis: >\n      rp-LOFO 双重验证（Llama + Gemma 均 F1≥0.70）建立了对 Gemma rp=1.1 纳入 main results 的\n      statistical justification。Reference features 的 rp-invariance 是关键理论洞见：\n      depth signal 的 robust component 不依赖 generator 的 sampling hyperparameters，\n      因为它由 recursive generation 的 information-theoretic 属性（而非 token-level 选择策略）决定。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"670f01e8-9a77-4683-a438-fb4d9dd8cb5c","total_cost_usd":1.3473643499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50944,"cache_read_input_tokens":141033,"output_tokens":26225,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50944,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":19264,"cache_read_input_tokens":46198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":23877,"outputTokens":10566,"cacheReadInputTokens":1039571,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97707,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30279785,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":26225,"cacheReadInputTokens":141033,"cacheCreationInputTokens":50944,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0445665,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c90cc2f9-1466-4e33-93a6-a8a147b5bd9d"}
